1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,696
When someone types the address of your site, the home page is the

2
00:00:04,696 --> 00:00:06,102
first thing they see.

3
00:00:06,102 --> 00:00:09,694
In this video, you choose which page that is, and you change it

4
00:00:09,694 --> 00:00:11,100
whenever you need to.

5
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,091
The home page is the page a visitor sees at the address of

6
00:00:19,091 --> 00:00:21,157
your site, with nothing after it.

7
00:00:21,157 --> 00:00:25,660
The Home Route feature sends every visit to that address to the page you chose.

8
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:31,035
The Autoroute feature gives content items their own address, called a permalink.

9
00:00:31,035 --> 00:00:34,638
It also adds a Set as homepage checkbox to the editor, so you

10
00:00:34,638 --> 00:00:37,380
choose the home page from the content itself.

11
00:00:38,130 --> 00:00:43,221
A content type, such as Article, defines what an item contains and is built from parts.

12
00:00:43,221 --> 00:00:47,163
A type offers the checkbox when it has the Autoroute part and that

13
00:00:47,163 --> 00:00:50,119
part's Show homepage options setting is checked.

14
00:00:50,119 --> 00:00:53,130
Your role also needs the Set homepage permission.

15
00:00:57,316 --> 00:01:00,684
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for Home Route.

16
00:01:00,684 --> 00:01:05,343
This feature, in the Infrastructure category, opens the page you chose as the

17
00:01:05,343 --> 00:01:08,936
home page whenever someone visits the address of the site.

18
00:01:09,418 --> 00:01:13,066
Autoroute, in the Navigation category, depends on Home Route.

19
00:01:13,066 --> 00:01:16,932
Both are enabled on this site, and Autoroute is the one that adds

20
00:01:16,932 --> 00:01:18,728
the checkbox to the editor.

21
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:25,945
Only some content types offer the checkbox.

22
00:01:25,945 --> 00:01:31,233
Let's open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit the Article type.

23
00:01:31,686 --> 00:01:34,904
Among its parts, Autoroute has its own Edit button.

24
00:01:34,904 --> 00:01:38,406
The settings of this part include Show homepage options.

25
00:01:38,869 --> 00:01:42,230
Show homepage options is already checked for Article.

26
00:01:42,230 --> 00:01:47,357
Its hint says the checkbox is only visible to users with the appropriate permission.

27
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:50,889
A separate video covers the other settings of this part.

28
00:01:55,118 --> 00:01:57,533
On this site, the home page is the Blog.

29
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:00,158
Let's make an article the home page instead.

30
00:02:00,611 --> 00:02:07,431
Let's open Content, Content Items, and edit the article called Welcome to Juniper Lane Studio.

31
00:02:07,896 --> 00:02:12,669
Under the Permalink field, the editor shows the Set as homepage checkbox.

32
00:02:12,669 --> 00:02:16,656
Its hint says the change applies once the item is published.

33
00:02:17,145 --> 00:02:20,220
Let's check Set as homepage, and select Publish.

34
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:23,695
A message confirms that the Article has been published.

35
00:02:24,156 --> 00:02:26,291
Let's visit the address of the site.

36
00:02:26,291 --> 00:02:28,476
The home page is the Welcome article.

37
00:02:28,936 --> 00:02:32,802
In the editor of the article, a note replaces the checkbox:

38
00:02:32,802 --> 00:02:35,656
This content item is the current homepage.

39
00:02:39,911 --> 00:02:43,660
To choose another page, edit that item the same way.

40
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:48,121
Let's open the Blog, check Set as homepage, and select Publish.

41
00:02:48,578 --> 00:02:52,318
At the address of the site, the Blog is the home page again.

42
00:02:52,318 --> 00:02:56,908
A site has one home page, so the Welcome article no longer holds that role.

43
00:02:57,371 --> 00:03:01,785
In the editor of the Welcome article, the Set as homepage checkbox is

44
00:03:01,785 --> 00:03:04,021
back, ready for the next change.

45
00:03:08,253 --> 00:03:11,789
The checkbox also needs the Set homepage permission.

46
00:03:11,789 --> 00:03:14,655
The Administrator role has it by default.

47
00:03:14,655 --> 00:03:18,983
For another role, open Access Control, Roles, and edit that role.

48
00:03:19,485 --> 00:03:23,812
Let's edit the Editor role and search the permissions for homepage.

49
00:03:23,812 --> 00:03:29,205
Set homepage is listed under Autoroute, and the Allow checkbox grants it to the role.

50
00:03:31,205 --> 00:03:34,061
Choosing the home page takes one checkbox:

51
00:03:34,061 --> 00:03:39,296
Set as homepage, in the editor of the content item that visitors should see first.

52
00:03:39,296 --> 00:03:43,818
Home Route opens that page for every visit to the address of the site.

53
00:03:43,818 --> 00:03:45,365
Thanks for watching.

